---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const M = "server/src/iki_server/runs/models.py";
const SV = "server/src/iki_server/runs/services.py";
const Q = "server/src/iki_server/runs/queue.py";
const R = "server/src/iki_server/runs/results.py";
const I = "server/src/iki_server/runs/included.py";
const RU = "server/src/iki_server/runs/reuse.py";

const H = {
  short: "What a run fixes, and what it can prove",
  how: "What a run pins at launch",
  rules: "Code, results, reuse, reproduction and kept files",
  ref: "Code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "attempt", label: "What each attempt receives" },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      At launch a run pins everything its results depend on: the plugin's commit, the action as
      installed, params, settings, reference data builds, an image if one is bound, a seed, each
      input at its revision, and each record its inputs' references name, at its revision. Every
      attempt runs that code on those records and nothing newer. Its results are checked against
      its own copy of the action and written all or nothing, as revisions that name the run. So a
      run's record says exactly what it read and ran, an identical run can reuse its results, and
      any run can be reproduced exactly (<Adr n={[35, 44, 47, 57, 105]} />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Pin</th><th>Kept as</th><th>What it's for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Plugin version and commit</td><td><code>ActionRun.plugin_version</code>, <code>plugin_sha</code></td><td>Only a worker with that code leases it; reuse and reproduction need the same commit.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The action</td><td><code>ActionRun.spec</code></td><td>Results are checked against it, not the action installed now.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Params and settings</td><td><code>params</code>, <code>plugin_settings</code></td><td>What the command gets; a file param counts in the reuse key by its content.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Reference data builds</td><td><code>volumes</code></td><td>Only a machine that mounts those builds may run it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A bound image</td><td><code>environment_image</code></td><td>Only a worker launched for that image leases it (<PageLink to="Licensed images" />).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>A seed</td><td><code>seed</code></td><td>Given as <code>IKI_SEED</code>, and again when it's reproduced.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Each input</td><td><code>RunInput</code>: entity, revision, registry entry revision</td><td>What it read, append-only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Each included reference</td><td><code>RunInclusion</code>: input, position, field, index, entity, revision</td><td>What it read through its inputs' references, append-only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Unreadable positions</td><td><code>reference_mask</code></td><td>Typed reference positions the project couldn't identify at launch: the worker gets <code>unreadable</code> there.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Retries and timeout</td><td><code>timeout</code>, <code>max_attempts</code>, <code>retry_on</code></td><td>How long each attempt may run, and when it's retried.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      <Path p={SV} sym="def _queue(" />, <Path p={SV} sym="def _made(" />, <Path p={M} sym="class ActionRun(" />,{" "}
      <Path p={M} sym="class RunInput(" />, <Path p={M} sym="class RunInclusion(" />, <Path
        p={I}
        sym="def reference_mask("
      />
    </p>

    <h3 id="attempt">What each attempt receives</h3>
    <p>
      Each lease builds the command's input document from the pins, through one function used for
      launch, reuse and every lease: each record at its pinned revision, its included records under{" "}
      <code>included</code>, and <code>unreadable</code> at the masked positions. It refuses if a
      pinned record was purged, or if the run's project can no longer read every record, reference
      and file param the command would receive. A lease that's refused ends the attempt with a
      generic reason, before the worker sees anything (<Adr n={[66, 105]} />, <Path
        p={I}
        sym="def manifest("
      />, <Path p={Q} sym="def lease(" />). The marker and the access check are on <PageLink
        to="Unreadable references"
      />. A retry reads the same pins, masked positions included.
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="A worker runs only the code the run was launched with" open>
        <p>
          The lease matches the job to workers that have the plugin at the run's commit and have
          built its environment; the worker checks again before it starts. Plugin code from a local
          directory has no commit, so a worker that fetched it names the bundle, and leases none of
          that plugin's jobs once another is installed. Each attempt records the environment build's
          digest (<Adr n="0047" />, <Path p={Q} sym="def _runnable(" />, <Path
            p="worker/crates/iki-worker/src/plugins.rs"
            sym="pub fn for_run("
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Results are written all or nothing">
        <p>
          The output is kept as a <code>RunOutput</code> whatever happens. It may update only the
          inputs, records and fields the action declares, and create only its declared types, and may
          attach only the run's own uploads, its file params' files and its inputs' files. Then, in
          one transaction, values are checked against the types installed now and written as the
          launcher, with <code>via="run"</code>, after checking the launcher's access again (<Adr
            n="0044"
          />, <Path p={R} sym="def checked(" />, <Path p={R} sym="def write(" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          An output that doesn't fit fails the run (<code>invalid_output</code>), or rejects it
          (<code>schema_changed</code>) if the plugin changed meanwhile. One that fits but can't be
          written now is rejected: an entity archived, the launcher's access gone, or an update with{" "}
          <code>require_unchanged</code> to a record changed since the run read it. None is retried
          (<Path p={Q} sym="def outcome(" />). A run's new records can refer to one another by key
          (<Adr n="0064" />), and a creates file is checked in chunks of 10,000 lines, staged with
          COPY, then written in one <code>INSERT … SELECT</code> (<Adr n="0056" />, <Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/runs/imports.py"
            sym="CHUNK_LINES = 10_000"
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Provenance">
        <p>
          Each record a run touched gets a <code>RunEffect</code>: created, updated or reused, and the
          revision it made, so a value's provenance leads to the run. Each new record gets{" "}
          <code>Lineage</code> to the inputs it was made from, at the revisions read (<Adr
            n={[35, 106]}
          />, <Path p={M} sym="class RunEffect(" />, <Path p={M} sym="class Lineage(" />). Revisions
          themselves are on <PageLink to="Revisions and history" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Reuse">
        <p>
          A deterministic action from a pinned commit gets a reuse key: the SHA-256 of the action, the
          plugin commit, params (a file by its content), settings, each input's id, revision, type
          and schema version, included references at their revisions, the reference mask, the
          image's digest, and the setup build of each volume. The seed never counts. Local plugin
          code is never reused (<Path p={RU} sym="def key(" />, <Path p={RU} sym="def with_volumes(" />).
        </p>
        <p>
          The newest run with that key that succeeded, ran itself, and is in a project the launcher
          can read is reused, if none of what it made is archived or kept to its project, and it
          made no more than 10,000 records. The new run ends succeeded at once, naming it, and those
          records are linked into its project (<Path p={RU} sym="def find(" />, <Path
            p={RU}
            sym="def reuse("
          />). When it's decided is on <PageLink to="Launching a run" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Exact reproduction">
        <p>
          <code>POST /api/v1/runs/{"{ref}"}/reproduce</code> queues a copy with the same action as
          launched, params, settings, inputs and inclusions at their revisions, mask and seed. It's
          refused if the plugin version or commit, the bound image or a pinned build differs or is
          gone, if a pinned record was purged, or if the person can't read what it read or it has left
          the project. A run that reused another's results reproduces that one. Its output is
          compared, not written (<Path p={SV} sym="def reproduce(" />, <Path p={RU} sym="def blocked(" />,{" "}
          <Path p={RU} sym="def compare(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Checkpoints and artifacts">
        <p>
          A checkpointable action's directory is uploaded every ten minutes if it changed, and once
          more on an ending the run is retried for; the next attempt is leased only once its
          checkpoint has been checked, and its worker restores it first (<Adr n="0069" />, <Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/runs/checkpoints.py"
            sym="def ready_to_resume("
          />). Files matching <code>artifacts.keep</code> are kept for the action's retention,
          success or failure; then their bytes are deleted and the record stays (<Adr n="0068" />,{" "}
          <Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/artifacts.py" />). Both are stored as <PageLink
            to="Where data is stored"
          /> describes.
        </p>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <div class="refs">
      <div>
        <h3>Where</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Path p={I} /></li>
          <li><Path p={RU} /></li>
          <li><Path p={R} /></li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/imports.py" /></li>
          <li><Path p="server/src/iki_server/runs/setups.py" /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Decisions</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><Adr n="0044" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0047" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0057" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0066" title /></li>
          <li><Adr n="0105" title /></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
